{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-844993f8d50c81a7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n3\tepic_count: 3\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8008 — Inference-Aware Autoscaling for llm-d KEDA primitives\n11\t\n12\tParent strategy: RHAISTRAT-8008 (priority: Critical, status: Refinement)\n13\t\n14\t## Triage Outcome\n15\t\n16\tFull decomposition (not below-threshold, not docs-only). The strategy is M-sized (2-3 sprints), spans\n17\tmultiple components (KServe llmisvc-controller, odh-model-controller, Documentation), multiple teams\n18\t(Serving team, Documentation team), and multiple architecturally distinct work streams: controller\n19\timplementation in the kserve repo, a separate reconciler in the odh-model-controller repo, and\n20\tsubstantive documentation authoring (decision guide, configuration recipes, troubleshooting).\n21\t\n22\tStaff Engineer Input section contains only template placeholder text — no overrides to log.\n23\t\n24\t## Investigation Scan\n25\t\n26\tAll unknowns were collected from the open questions table, risks, assumptions, and pending process\n27\tgates, then evaluated against the decision rule (\"does the answer change which downstream epics exist\n28\tor what they do?\"). None qualified for an Investigation epic:\n29\t\n30\t| Unknown | Source | Disposition |\n31\t|---------|--------|-------------|\n32\t| Does upstream PR kserve/kserve#5839 require downstream adaptation beyond the authentication context? | Open Questions | Acceptance criterion on the odh-model-controller epic — the reconciler work proceeds the same way (follow the existing `kserve_keda_reconciler` pattern); any additional RBAC/TLS adjustments are discovered and folded in during implementation (fix-and-retry, not a gate) |\n33\t| Target p50/p95 for scale-from-zero