cumentation\"]\n76\t    E001 --> E002\n77\t    E001 --> E003\n78\t    E002 --> E003\n79\t```\n80\t\n81\t## DAG Justification\n82\t\n83\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n84\t|------|------|-----------|\n85\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | E001 produces the `spec.scaling.keda` API fields / CRD shape that the odh-model-controller reconciler's code builds against (it must watch and interpret the new LLMInferenceService scaling fields). Consuming implementation is serial after the producing one. |\n86\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs last) | `docs-authoring` epic is blocked by all Implementation epics — docs describe what was built. |\n87\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 11 (docs last) | The OpenShift authentication flow (TriggerAuthentication reference in trigger definitions) must be documented as built. |\n88\t\n89\tNo konflux-onboarding, repo-onboarding, or license-validation epics: both target repositories are\n90\texisting in-platform components with established build pipelines. No konflux-onboarding → general\n91\tedge exists, so no Rule 25 \"build pipeline green\" AC is required beyond normal CI.\n92\t\n93\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n94\t\n95\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Coverage |\n96\t|-----|----------|---------|----------|\n97\t| HLR1: Standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers without WVA | P0 | E001, E002 | E001 delivers the API/validation/controller path; E002 delivers the OpenShift authentication context that makes Prometheus-type triggers (the primary supported trigger source) work |\n98\t| HLR2: Mutual exclusivity of WVA and standalone KEDA via CEL validation | P0 | E001 | API validation changes |\n99\t| HLR3: Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` (both paths) | P0 | E001 | ScaledObject construction in the scaling controller |\n100\t| HLR4: Scale-from-zero (WVA via EPP queue metrics; standalone KEDA via user triggers) | P0 | E001, E003 | E001 delivers the trigger-driven mechanism; E003 documents recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP queue metrics (risk mitigation) |\n101\t| HLR5: Disaggregated prefill/decode independent scaling (both paths) | P0 | E001 | Phase-specific ScaledObjects + actuator consistency validation |\n102\t| HLR6: Scaling events visible with signal attribution | P1 | E001 | Scaling status conditions for both paths (bundled — same implementation surface) |\n103\t| HLR7: Decision-guide documentation covering both paths | P1 | E003 | Full docs scope |\n104\t\n105\tNo orphaned HLRs; every HLR maps to at least one epic.\n106\t\n107\t## Health Warnings\n108\t\n109\t1. **All strategy process gates pending**: Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding, Licence\n110\t   Validation, Accelerator/Package Support, Documentation Support, UXD Support, and Performance Team\n111\t   Support are all \"Pending human review\" and the strategy status is Refinement. The decomposition\n112\t   proceeds, but human verification of these gates is required before implementation starts.\n113\t2. **Docs epic priority derivation**: E003 is P0 solely because the strategy frontmatter priority is\n114\t   Critical and the docs-authoring exception mandates Critical→P0. Its only HLR is P1. Planners\n115\t   should not read the P0 as implementation-blocking urgency.\n116\t3. **External-team inputs to documentation unresolved**: the scale-from-zero p50/p95 target (llm-d\n117\t   team) and Prometheus capacity guidance (Performance/PSAP team) are open; the docs epic carries ACs\n118\t   to incorporate them, and a revision pass may be needed once they land.\n119\t4. **Scalability NFR has no measurable RHOAI target** — the strategy itself flags this (number of\n120\t   concurrent ScaledObjects unspecified in RFE or architecture context).\n121\t5. **Upstream dependency timing**: kserve/kserve#5839 is in progress. Handled via the documented\n122\t   fallback (carry the patch downstream) rather than tiered delivery — see below.\n123\t\n124\t## Tiered Delivery\n125\t\n126\tEvaluated per Step 5.5 and **not applied**. The single external dependency with uncertain timing\n127\t(upstream PR kserve/kserve#5839) has a viable, strategy-documented fallback: RHOAI carries the patch\n128\tdownstream with backport once merged. Because the fallback keeps the llmisvc-controller epic\n129\texecutable regardless of upstream timing, splitting into Tier 1 (independent) / Tier 2 (gated) work\n130\twould add structure without unblocking anything. The fallback is recorded as an acceptance criterion\n131\ton E001 (Rule 21: viable fallback → AC, not separate epic).\n132\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a56a4f290a28a50c","agent_id":"aa4d7dee2893ef04c","session_id":"41f0b542-dbb8-4d5e-a349-930fe2b66c78","uuid":"c711b76c-ab86-44d3-b7f6-1ac53ad03025","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:05.825Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-844993f8d50c81a7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8008 decomposition"}
