nfigurations using EPP queue metrics (risk mitigation) |\n101\t| HLR5: Disaggregated prefill/decode independent scaling (both paths) | P0 | E001 | Phase-specific ScaledObjects + actuator consistency validation |\n102\t| HLR6: Scaling events visible with signal attribution | P1 | E001 | Scaling status conditions for both paths (bundled — same implementation surface) |\n103\t| HLR7: Decision-guide documentation covering both paths | P1 | E003 | Full docs scope |\n104\t\n105\tNo orphaned HLRs; every HLR maps to at least one epic.\n106\t\n107\t## Health Warnings\n108\t\n109\t1. **All strategy process gates pending**: Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding, Licence\n110\t   Validation, Accelerator/Package Support, Documentation Support, UXD Support, and Performance Team\n111\t   Support are all \"Pending human review\" and the strategy status is Refinement. The decomposition\n112\t   proceeds, but human verification of these gates is required before implementation starts.\n113\t2. **Docs epic priority derivation**: E003 is P0 solely because the strategy frontmatter priority is\n114\t   Critical and the docs-authoring exception mandates Critical→P0. Its only HLR is P1. Planners\n115\t   should not read the P0 as implementation-blocking urgency.\n116\t3. **External-team inputs to documentation unresolved**: the scale-from-zero p50/p95 target (llm-d\n117\t   team) and Prometheus capacity guidance (Performance/PSAP team) are open; the docs epic carries ACs\n118\t   to incorporate them, and a revision pass may be needed once they land.\n119\t4. **Scalability NFR has no measurable RHOAI target** — the strategy itself flags this (number of\n120\t   concurrent ScaledObjects unspecified in RFE or architecture context).\n121\t5. **Upstream dependency timing**: kserve/kserve#5839 is in progress. Handled via the documented\n122\t   fallback (carry the patch downstream) rather than tiered delivery — see below.\n123\t\n124\t## Tiered Delivery\n125\t\n126\tEvaluated per Step 5