{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a985f915188a8a58","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E001\n3\ttitle: Standalone KEDA autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in the llmisvc-controller\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: Serving Orchestration\n6\tteam: Serving team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies: []\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 0\n16\t  external_dependency: -1\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Standalone KEDA autoscaling path for LLMInferenceService in the llmisvc-controller\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers standalone KEDA autoscaling as a first-class path for LLMInferenceService in the\n34\tKServe llmisvc-controller, following the upstream design in kserve/kserve#5646 and its implementation\n35\tPR kserve/kserve#5839. Users configure KEDA triggers directly in the LLMInferenceService spec without\n36\tdeploying WVA (Workload Variant Autoscaler), bringing LLMInferenceService to feature parity with\n37\tv1beta1 InferenceService. The two autoscaling paths (WVA-mediated and standalone KEDA) are mutually\n38\texclusive and both support scale-to/from-zero and independent prefill/decode scaling for\n39\tdisaggregated deployments.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- **API type changes** in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_types.go`: add a standalone\n44\t  KEDA spec at the ScalingSpec level containing `pollingInterval`, `cooldownPeriod`, and a `triggers`\n45\t  field for user-defined KEDA trigger definitions (type, metadata map). Relax the CEL validation from\n46\t  requiring `wva` to requiring at least one of `wva` or `keda`.\n47\t- **Validation changes** in `pkg/apis/serving/v1alpha2/llm_inference_service_validation.go`: enforce\n48\t  mutual exclusivity (at-least-one and at-most-one of `wva`/`keda`), validate trigger completeness,\n49\t  and enforce actuator consistency for disaggregated deployments (both prefill and decode phases must\n50\t  use the same scaling path, per architecture overlay 0011). Standalone KEDA remains mutually\n51\t  exclusive with static `spec.replicas`.\n52\t- **Controller changes** in `pkg/controller/v1alpha2/llmisvc/scaling.go`: branch on which path is\n53\t  configured. The standalone KEDA path creates a ScaledObject using user-provided triggers\n54\t  (supporting Resource, External, and PodMetric trigger types, per the v1beta1 KEDA reconciler\n55\t  reference implementation at\n56\t  `pkg/controller/v1beta1/inferenceservice/reconcilers/keda/keda_reconciler.go`) and skips\n57\t  VariantAutoscaling CR creation entirely.\n58\t- **Scale-to-zero**: standalone KEDA ScaledObjects are created with `idleReplicaCount: 0` so idle\n59\t  deployments release GPU capacity (identical behavior to the WVA path).\n60\t- **Disaggregated scaling**: phase-specific ScaledObjects for prefill and decode pools so each scales\n61\t  independently based on its load profile.\n62\t- **Scaling status conditions** for both paths, with scaling decision events visible via KEDA\n63\t  ScaledObject events for the standalone path (signal attribution).\n64\t- **Backwards compatibility**: static deployments with no `spec.scaling` continue unchanged; existing\n65\t  LLMInferenceService CRs with `spec.scaling.wva` continue unchanged; the standalone KEDA path is\n66\t  additive.\n67\t- **Upstream integration**: land kserve/kserve#5839 in RHOAI's KServe (upstream merge + backport), or\n68\t  carry the patch downstream if upstream acceptance is delayed.\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` configured with user-defined triggers and no\n73\t  WVA deployed, when the trigger condition is met (e.g., Prometheus query threshold exceeded), then\n74\t  the deployment scales up, measured by KEDA ScaledObject status showing active and Deployment\n75\t  replica count increasing.\n76\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with both `spec.scaling.wva` and `spec.scaling.keda` set, when the CR\n77\t  is submitted, then the API server rejects it with a CEL validation error indicating mutual\n78\t  exclusivity.\n79\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with `spec.scaling.keda` and no `spec.scaling.wva`, when the\n80\t  llmisvc-controller reconciles, then no VariantAutoscaling CR is created and a ScaledObject with\n81\t  user-provided triggers is created, measured by `kubectl get variantautoscalings` returning empty\n82\t  and `kubectl get scaledobjects` returning a ScaledObject with the user's triggers.\n83\t- Given an LLMInferenceService with KEDA and `idleReplicaCount: 0`, when no requests are received for\n84\t  the cooldown period, then the deployment scales to zero, measured by Deployment replica count\n85\t  reaching 0 and KEDA ScaledObject status showing idle. This also validates the assumption that KEDA\n86\t  ScaledObject with `idleReplicaCount: 0` correctly pauses and resumes scaling for LLM inference\n87\t  workloads.\n88\t- Given a disaggregated LLMInferenceService with separate scaling configs, when prefill pods reach\n89\t  saturation while decode pods remain below threshold, then only the prefill pool scales up,\n90\t  measured by independent scaling resource status for prefill and decode roles.\n91\t- Given a deployment with autoscaling active, when Prometheus metrics become unavailable, then the\n92\t  deployment holds its current replica count, measured by replica count remaining stable during the\n93\t  metric outage.\n94\t- Static deployments with no autoscaling configured continue to serve identically, measured by no\n95\t  VariantAutoscaling, HPA, or ScaledObject resources created for deployments without `spec.scaling`;\n96\t  existing WVA-mediated autoscaling behavior is unchanged (backwards compatibility).\n97\t- Scale-from-zero for the standalone path is exercised end-to-end with a user-configured trigger\n98\t  (e.g., Prometheus query on EPP flow control queue metrics), including validation that EPP flow\n99\t  control queue metrics are reliably available while model pods are at zero replicas (EPP itself\n100\t  remains running).\n101\t- Scaling decision events are emitted with signal attribution (KEDA ScaledObject events for the\n102\t  standalone path; WVA events for the WVA path), and scaling status conditions report correctly for\n103\t  both paths.\n104\t- Upstream PR kserve/kserve#5839 is merged and backported into RHOAI's KServe, or the patch is\n105\t  carried downstream with backport once merged (fallback path if upstream acceptance is delayed).\n106\t- Unit and integration tests cover both autoscaling paths, mutual exclusivity validation, and the\n107\t  disaggregated topology (standalone KEDA × 2 topologies per the effort estimate).\n108\t\n109\t## HLR Traceability\n110\t\n111\t- HLR1 [P0]: LLMInferenceService supports standalone KEDA autoscaling with user-defined triggers\n112\t  without requiring WVA deployment (kserve/kserve#5646)\n113\t- HLR2 [P0]: The two autoscaling paths are mutually exclusive at the API level with CEL validation\n114\t  enforcing at-least-one and at-most-one\n115\t- HLR3 [P0]: Scale-to-zero via KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` to release GPU capacity (both paths)\n116\t- HLR4 [P0]: Scale-from-zero (standalone KEDA via user-configured triggers)\n117\t- HLR5 [P0]: Disaggregated prefill and decode pools scale independently (both paths)\n118\t- HLR6 [P1]: Scaling events visible to operators with signal attribution\n119\t\n120\t## Risks\n121\t\n122\t- Upstream PR acceptance timeline (kserve/kserve#5839) — mitigated by the carry-downstream fallback\n123\t  acceptance criterion above.\n124\t- Standalone KEDA scale-from-zero reliability with misconfigured triggers — mitigated by\n125\t  documentation of recommended trigger configurations (covered by the documentation epic scope) and\n126\t  example ScaledObject templates.\n127\t- EPP flow control queue metrics availability at zero replicas — validated as an acceptance criterion\n128\t  above.\n129\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9306e95e37e6bc93","agent_id":"aedd93bf8910f31f6","session_id":"41f0b542-dbb8-4d5e-a349-930fe2b66c78","uuid":"27015dc9-124c-402e-9fac-e679332f28ab","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:22:31.224Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a985f915188a8a58","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008"}
