{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-86d50eb5915ed2a5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8008-E003\n3\ttitle: 'LLMInferenceService autoscaling documentation: decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8008\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Documentation team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8008-E002\n13\tai_signals:\n14\t  change_specificity: 1\n15\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n16\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n17\t  existing_foundation: 1\n18\t  open_questions: -1\n19\t  external_dependency: 0\n20\t  human_process_gates: -1\n21\t  repo_access: 1\n22\t  architecture_claims: 1\n23\tinvestigation_signals: null\n24\tai_implementability: High\n25\tai_implementability_score: 3\n26\tjira_key: null\n27\tbranch: null\n28\tgated_by: null\n29\tgate_failure_impact: null\n30\t---\n31\t# LLMInferenceService autoscaling documentation: decision guide, recipes, troubleshooting\n32\t\n33\t## Description\n34\t\n35\tThis epic delivers the documentation for LLMInferenceService autoscaling, covering both autoscaling\n36\tpaths (WVA-mediated and standalone KEDA) and static allocation. It provides a decision guide for\n37\tchoosing between the paths, configuration recipes per workload shape, troubleshooting guidance, a\n38\tsupported configuration matrix, and the prerequisite/operator guidance needed to run standalone KEDA\n39\ton OpenShift (KEDA installation, TriggerAuthentication for Prometheus queries).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- **Decision guide**: use-case-based recommendations for WVA-mediated autoscaling vs. standalone KEDA\n44\t  vs. static allocation (mitigates the \"two scaling paths in a single CRD may confuse operators\"\n45\t  risk; CEL validation error messages complement it).\n46\t- **Configuration recipes per workload shape**, including the RFE's example scenario (a coding\n47\t  assistant deployment that scales prefill and decode pools during business hours and releases GPUs\n48\t  overnight).\n49\t- **Scale-to-zero and scale-from-zero guidance**: KEDA `idleReplicaCount: 0` configuration,\n50\t  recommended scale-from-zero trigger configurations using EPP flow control queue metrics, and\n51\t  example ScaledObject templates (mitigates the standalone KEDA scale-from-zero reliability risk).\n52\t- **Realistic cold start expectations** for scale-from-zero latency, referencing the fast model\n53\t  startup RFEs (RHAIRFE-7753, RHAIRFE-7599, RHAIRFE-7139) and headroom configuration for\n54\t  latency-sensitive workloads.\n55\t- **KEDA prerequisite documentation**: RHOAI does not auto-install KEDA (platform policy overlay\n56\t  0008); document KEDA as a prerequisite with installation guidance referencing the GitOps repository\n57\t  (ODH-ADR-0007).\n58\t- **Authenticated Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift**: instructions for operators to reference\n59\t  the TriggerAuthentication resource in their KEDA trigger definitions.\n60\t- **Disaggregated scaling guidance**: independent prefill/decode scaling configuration and the\n61\t  same-path (actuator consistency) requirement.\n62\t- **Supported configuration matrix** and **troubleshooting paths** (including behavior when\n63\t  Prometheus metrics become unavailable — replica count holds steady).\n64\t- **Observability guidance**: where to see scaling decision events (KEDA ScaledObject events for the\n65\t  standalone path; WVA events for the WVA path) and ScaledObject metrics for dashboard integration.\n66\t- **Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments** (e.g., polling-interval impact at\n67\t  large GPU fleet scale) — incorporating input from the Performance/PSAP team once available.\n68\t- **Scale-from-zero latency targets**: incorporate the p50/p95 target (the RFE telemetry section\n69\t  references a 60-second p50 threshold) and resulting headroom pre-scaling recommendations, based on\n70\t  input from the llm-d team once available.\n71\t\n72\t## Acceptance Criteria\n73\t\n74\t- A published decision guide covers WVA-mediated autoscaling, standalone KEDA, and static allocation\n75\t  with use-case-based recommendations.\n76\t- Configuration recipes exist for both paths, including scale-to-zero, scale-from-zero (with\n77\t  recommended EPP queue metric trigger configurations and example ScaledObject templates), and\n78\t  disaggregated prefill/decode scaling.\n79\t- KEDA is documented as a prerequisite with installation guidance referencing the GitOps repository\n80\t  (RHOAI does not auto-install KEDA).\n81\t- Operators are instructed how to reference the TriggerAuthentication resource for authenticated\n82\t  Prometheus/Thanos queries on OpenShift.\n83\t- Troubleshooting content covers common failure modes (misconfigured triggers failing the\n84\t  zero-to-one transition, Prometheus metric outages holding replica count) and a supported\n85\t  configuration matrix is published.\n86\t- Scale-from-zero latency expectations and headroom recommendations incorporate the agreed p50/p95\n87\t  target from the llm-d team (open question; content updated or a revision pass scheduled once the\n88\t  target lands).\n89\t- Prometheus capacity guidance for fleet-scale deployments incorporates Performance/PSAP team input\n90\t  (open question; content updated or a revision pass scheduled once available).\n91\t- All content is technically reviewed against the implemented behavior of both autoscaling paths and\n92\t  the OpenShift authentication flow (mandatory technical review).\n93\t\n94\t## HLR Traceability\n95\t\n96\t- HLR7 [P1]: Well-lit path documentation covers both autoscaling paths with decision guide,\n97\t  configuration recipes per workload shape, and troubleshooting\n98\t- HLR4 [P0] (documentation portion): scale-from-zero guidance for the standalone path — recommended\n99\t  trigger configurations using EPP queue metrics and example ScaledObject templates (risk mitigation\n100\t  for standalone KEDA scale-from-zero reliability)\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9306e95e37e6bc93","agent_id":"aedd93bf8910f31f6","session_id":"41f0b542-dbb8-4d5e-a349-930fe2b66c78","uuid":"467855d2-14b6-430f-9753-30089d8ce492","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:22:32.684Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86d50eb5915ed2a5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8008"}
